Yes, loops are used to repeat a block of code a certain number of times.  For example, you might want to print out a message to the console a certain number of times.  In C, you can use a for loop to do this.  The syntax is like this:

for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    cout << "This will be printed 5 times" << endl;
}

In this example, the variable "i" starts out at 0, and the condition is that "i" is less than 5.  So, the loop runs 5 times, and each time the value of "i" is printed.

